# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch commit and merge messages
#
# Long commit messages get written to a file and passed with `git commit -F`,
# because a shell heredoc mangles them and a message worth writing is worth not
# retyping. They are drafts, not repository content - .mergemsg reached main by
# being untracked-but-not-ignored on the one day somebody ran `git add -A`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.commitmsg
.mergemsg

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Benchmark exports
#
# Keep a run you want in the report under data/exports/ and commit it there, on
# purpose. What this ignores is the default filename the export script writes
# into the repository root.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/benchmark-*.csv

